  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PET Recycling in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The demand for recycled PET is bigger than the offer. In Tanzania waste disposal is not regulated, waste mostly ends up on streets. High value PET bottles are making up a large part of the waste. By collecting and importing this PET to Europe, Tanzania will have help with ending plastic waste and create an economy around the export of plastics, by which job creation will take place. PET Recycling Africa works with a local partner. On land of this local partner a factory will be build where the plastics will be processed. Machinery has been shipped to Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
